  "coverage": [
    "All eight operational states, all three filters, group titles, row state/technician/task/time, known status labels and location/GPS content through the real five-language selector. Initial320/390/1440 matrix, critical/completed/fallback and empty-filter cases at320.",
    "Same actual button/leaf nodes and focus after each locale, exact row index/order/classes, active filter, typed visit, controls, inputs, tokens, own raw local data, complete outbox and cw:tech-field session navigation records. Only language-preference PUTs allowed during each matrix; producers and SQL unchanged.",
    "REGULAR/EXTRA share the same number and have different pools. Real list clicks preserve their identity and the regular draft; an actual EXTRA offline water reminder appears only on the EXTRA row and moves it to the existing in-progress group. Original reminder and route-cache bytes are restored before fresh navigation.",
    "Known planned/start/travel/incomplete/completed states; regular completion through endAt retains the correction label. Unknown HTML/placeholder-like status remains literal. Literal pool/client/technician/address/zone, five-decimal coordinates, missing GPS, empty names/status/location, invalid start time and65 elapsed minutes.",
    "Source order remains the existing schedule order. Task type still uses the existing selected-draft rule for every row; elapsed time still uses each visit startAt. No changes to classification, grouping, rounding, address precedence, GPS validation, selection or physical confirmations.",
    "Empty route content translates while the list remains hidden by the existing free-mode policy. Empty visible filter groups remain usable. Persisted DONE filter survives an actual offline reload; subsequent row clicks retain typed navigation and the original draft.",
    "Existing modern-route recovery verifies account/day privacy, cache corruption and stale replies. Existing extra-reminder, modern-draft and browser-component regressions pass. New profiles retain9s locator/110s scenario/120s runner deadlines; no page errors or operational POST/PATCH/DELETE calls."
  ],
  "qaCorrections": [
    "Fixture expectations follow the actual API ordering (scheduled EXTRA before the late planned REGULAR) and preserve the server-provided literal zone placeholder -; truly absent location is tested separately in the valid offline fixture.",
    "Navigation-state byte comparison covers cw:tech-field session records. The generic page-context snapshot legitimately stores the selected language and scroll position, so it is not treated as unchanged locale-independent data.",
    "An empty route hides dayVisitsCard by existing policy. Its translations and hidden state are checked without clicking a hidden filter or claiming visible empty-card layout coverage.",
    "Readiness now also waits for the existing draft save/check phase to settle, alongside document/photo readiness, before assertions and subsequent selection. This follows the existing draft regression and retains the original timeout budgets."
  ],
